6294-Cut B of the arrival substrate (decision:design/arrival-sliceB-projections
6295-§Q3). The derived log is a byte-sorted projection of an arrival log, so two
6296-branches that both appended to their stores produce two files whose contents
6297-overlap and whose lines interleave — a textual three-way merge produces
6298-garbage, and git's built-in ``merge=union`` produces duplicate and
6299-interleaved lines in arbitrary order while detecting neither same-id
6300:divergence nor loss.
6301-
6302-This driver unions by **row id** over whole canonical lines and REFUSES the
6303-two cases a projection of an append-only log cannot honestly resolve.
6304-
6305-``libs/store`` is the maintenance-operations lib by charter, and a git driver
6306-is tooling over store artifacts rather than a runtime write path. **The sort
6307-rule and the line grammar live once in engine** — this module imports
6308-:func:`engine.arrival_projection.canonical_line` and
6309-:func:`~engine.arrival_projection.sort_key` rather than re-spelling them, so
6310-driver output and a fresh derivation cannot drift.
6311-
6312-**NON-NEGOTIABLE: the driver never opens a store and never touches an
6313-arrival log.** It reads three files and writes one.
6314-
6315-There is deliberately **no merge driver for ``.arrival``**. Two arrival logs
6316:cannot be merged textually — every record after the divergence point carries
6317-a ``prev`` chained to a different predecessor, so a textual union produces a
6318-file that refuses to walk. Combining two arrival lineages is a custody
6319-ceremony and its name is :func:`store.merge_store`.
6320-
6321-Registration rides wave 2: this cut adds no repo-root ``.gitattributes`` and
6322-changes no ``.gitignore`` line.
