6380-    """Map every row id in ``lines`` to the canonical line carrying it.
6381-
6382-    **The union key is the ROW ID, and identity is the whole canonical
6383-    line.** A batch line carries several ids and every one of them maps to
6384-    that same whole line — which is why the key cannot be a naive ``(t, id)``
6385-    pair read off the object: a batch has no single id, and the same row can
6386-    be a plain fact line on one side and ride inside a batch on the other.
6387:    Mapping id → whole line makes that a detectable divergence rather than a
6388-    silent duplicate.
6389-
6390-    Lines are CANONICALIZED before comparison, through engine's one spelling
6391-    of the grammar, so key order or whitespace noise cannot mint a false
6392-    conflict.
6393-    """
